course: dictionary
lesson: 1711
title: Cinnamon: a spice and a colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and it can be a different kind of word each time. Cinnamon can be a noun, a spice you cook with, or an adjective, a colour. The context tells you which. «Pepper, cinnamon, nutmeg and cloves came from Asia» is about spices, because pepper and nutmeg are spices too.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. «American black bears can be black, brown, cinnamon or even white» tells you cinnamon is a colour, because it sits in a list of colours. Swap your meaning in: a bear can be light reddish-brown, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Cinnamon for cooking goes into buns, apple pie, porridge and hot chocolate. Food words such as pie and porridge are the clues that cinnamon is the spice here, not the colour.
fact: Cinnamon can be a noun or an adjective, so check the sentence to see which job it does.
fact: As a spice, cinnamon is a sweet, warm-tasting brown powder or stick, used in cakes, buns and drinks.
fact: As a colour, cinnamon is a light reddish-brown, as in «cinnamon-coloured».
fact: Cinnamon is the inner bark of a tree, peeled and dried so it curls; Sri Lanka is famous for true cinnamon.
fact: Long ago, cinnamon was traded across the world, and it was never a safe thing to play with: never swallow spice powder as a dare, as it can make you choke.
exercise: «Pepper, cinnamon, nutmeg and cloves came from Asia and far islands.» In this sentence, what is cinnamon? | *A spice | Another name for a bear | A kind of cake | A colour of paint
exercise: «American black bears can be black, brown, cinnamon or even white.» What does cinnamon mean here? | A sweet, warm-tasting spice | A cake with apples | A bear that climbs trees | *A light reddish-brown colour
exercise: Lily says she put cinnamon in her hot chocolate, so cinnamon must be a colour. What clue shows it is a spice? | Hot chocolate is brown, so cinnamon is a colour | Hot chocolate is a tree | *Hot chocolate is a drink, and cinnamon goes into drinks as a spice | Hot chocolate is a bear
test: Where does cinnamon come from? | Fallen leaves | *The inner bark of a tree | A rock on the seabed | Cow's milk
test: Ella says her boots are cinnamon-coloured. What kind of word is cinnamon in that phrase? | *Adjective | Adverb | Noun | Verb
exam: Which sentence uses cinnamon as a spice? | The bear's fur was a cinnamon shade. | The cinnamon bear climbed the tall tree. | Her cinnamon scarf matched the autumn leaves. | *She sprinkled cinnamon on her apple pie.
